# .env.clinical.example
# ─────────────────────
# NON-SECRET configuration for docker-compose.clinical.yml. Copy to
# .env.clinical (git-ignored) and edit. NOTHING SECRET GOES IN THIS FILE: secrets
# are files under ./secrets, created by scripts/clinical-secrets.sh and read by
# the containers through <NAME>_FILE variables (see docs/CLINICAL_DEPLOYMENT.md).
#
# Use it with:  docker compose -f docker-compose.clinical.yml --env-file .env.clinical ...

# The ids the containers run as. The default (10001) works where file ownership
# is flattened (Docker Desktop). On a native Linux host set these to the owner of
# ./secrets -- `id -u` / `id -g` -- so that mode-0600 secret files are readable.
# CLINICAL_UID=10001
# CLINICAL_GID=10001

# Where the secret files live (default ./secrets, git-ignored).
# CLINICAL_SECRETS_DIR=./secrets

# The API is published on 127.0.0.1 only. This changes the port, not the address.
# CLINICAL_API_PORT=8000

# Addresses whose X-Forwarded-For / X-Forwarded-Proto uvicorn will believe.
# Leave unset unless a trusted reverse proxy sits in front, then set it to that
# proxy's EXPLICIT address or subnet (e.g. 172.30.0.5 or 172.30.0.0/29).
# NEVER "*": that lets any caller forge its own address into the audit log and
# the login throttle. The default (127.0.0.1) believes no one.
# CLINICAL_FORWARDED_ALLOW_IPS=

# The bundled database's name, and the images (pinned by digest in the compose file).
# CLINICAL_DB_NAME=clinical
# CLINICAL_IMAGE=geper-clinical:slim
# CLINICAL_TEST_IMAGE=geper-clinical:slim-test
# CLINICAL_POSTGRES_IMAGE=

# Off unless 1/true/yes: FastAPI's /docs, /redoc and /openapi.json. Leave it off
# anywhere that is not a developer's machine. To enable it, add the variable to
# the clinical-api service's environment in the compose file.
